  "term": "xerophthalmia",
  "definition": "Xerophthalmia is abnormal dryness of the eye’s surface because there are too few tears or too little conjunctival secretion. It can occur with vitamin A deficiency, eye injury, or problems that prevent the eyelids from fully closing.",
